<title>USA: U.S. details dairy export subsidies under DEIP.</title>
<headline>U.S. details dairy export subsidies under DEIP.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-10-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>The U.S. Agriculture Department said Friday it spent $78,000 in nonfat dry milk subsidies under the Dairy Export Incentive Program since October 1.</p>
<p>It spent a further $22,000 on cheese export subsidies in the same period. There were no whole milk powder or butterfat subsidies in the period.</p>
<p>Since July 1, spending on nonfat dry milk export subsidies was $461,000, with $44,000 spent on whole milk powder exports and $107,000 on cheese exports. There were no subsidized butterfat exports since July 1.</p>
<p>The United States has exported 516 tonnes of subsidized nonfat dry milk since July 1, 44 tonnes of whole milk powder and 110 tonnes of cheese.</p>
<p>There were no subsidized exports under the Export Enhancement Program, USDA said.</p>
<p>The figures were released as part of subsidy reporting under the Uruguay Round agreement.</p>
<p>-- Washington Commodities Desk (202) 898-8489</p>
</text>
